    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i'm a bit worried about the kitchen actually following through on the allergy stuff though. sometimes things get lost in translation between the office and the chefs. do you have any advice on how to make the instructions \"foolproof\" so there's no chance of cross-contamination during a busy service?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To ensure kitchen staff follows instructions, consider creating a detailed, step-by-step flowchart or checklist of allergen protocols. Have a manager or point person on site to oversee kitchen operations and provide real-time guidance. Also, consider conducting a pre-event drill with the chef and kitchen staff to review the allergy protocols and timeline, so everyone is on the same page. This can help identify potential pitfalls and prevent mistakes.",
      "source": "target",
